# rm309, the dancing margins (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm309
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rm_soren_kelpcot
written_by codex
title the dancing margins
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=scholar
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk marks_the_steps_of_a_dance_in_scrap_paper_margins
likes spiced_cider dancing market_bustle misty_dawns
dislikes haggling wet_floors
fears an_erased_signature a_wet_floor_during_a_turn
hopes an_archive_of_dances a_cabin_free_of_salt_damp
topics pastimes +0.5 work +0.4 festival +0.3
styles comfort=company gossip=precise refuse=firm tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# draws dancing feet in the margins of scrap paper, keeps a civil welcome for a new arrival, and demands an exact price before bargaining can begin.

words
oath! = Split quill and scuffed heel | Cider on the clean copy
saying! = Give each step its margin | One price leaves two feet free
stepleaf = my dancing margin | a register of steps
heelstamp = a fat dot of ink | a broad oval mark
toeline = a narrow dash | a sloped toe mark
pairrule = a line two fingers wide | a double-ruled margin
cupwarmth = the heat through my cup | the first fragrant steam
pegclip = a little wooden clip | a fork of springy wood
watercurl = a damp paper curl | a wrinkled edge
airfold = a loose open fold | a fold for airing
greycloth = a square of blotting cloth | a scrap of clean sleeve
marketnote = a note from a caller | a folded price slip
thintrack = two faint strokes | a pair of ghost marks

any
opinion @1 city for 1 : No other place has given me quite so many names for the turning of a lane, all settled by walking it together.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : Every new arrival gives a blank line in the register a reason to exist. A blank line makes thin reading.
opinion @1 houses for 1 : The roof over the records must be paid for by someone with more than a clerk's salary. I give the Houses credit for keeping old writing dry.
opinion @1 watch for 1 : When there's an argument over a boundary I'd like someone to keep the doorway clear while the paper's read.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : Lost callers don't stay strange once you've shown them the right turn and heard a little about the road before it.
opinion @1 times for 1 : I have clean paper for the work and cider when my feet are tired. Things stand tolerably well in my particular column.

grown
line @1 greet : Come take the unmarked space beside me.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Your name can wait, if you'd like to warm up first.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : The light's coming through the mist in ruled lines. Welcome.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : At this hour a greeting may come quietly off the page.
line @5 greet [self.working=yes] : Welcome. I'll put a weight on the open sheet.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Close enough for me to recognise your step alone.
line @1 again.open : Another line on the same page between us.
line @1 greet.return : Your words have come through legibly enough.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I heard a step I'd have entered in my margin.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : I've marked where I stopped. You have my ear.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : There's the voice I couldn't make out in the shadows.
line @1 farewell : A clear turn and a firm floor wherever you go.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll hold my place. Enjoy your stretch of road.
line @1 react.news : I'd like to hear the account in its proper order.
line @1 react.news.new : That's going into a previously blank margin.
line @1 react.news.known : Yes. The details fit the first account I had.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Was that the word on the original sheet?
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'd gladly take on the small business such a house hasn't time to do.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Something to put an extra spring in a returning step.
line @1 answer.how : I can still reckon with both my papers and my feet.
line @1 ask.how : Is there a comfortable measure to your day?
line @1 sympathise : A loss can leave more room than a wolf knows how to fill.
line @1 reassure : I'll take the first step beside you. The pace can be yours.
line @1 decline : I'd have to disclose a page that isn't mine to open.
line @1 accept_decline : We'll keep that entry folded out of sight.
line @1 thank : You've given a knotty entry its plain meaning.
line @1 deflect_thanks : It cost very little to draw the right line.
line @1 preclose : A blank margin has begun to nag at my memory.
line @1 accept_preclose : I'll let you turn back to your business.
line @1 ack : Duly understood.
scene drawdance
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dancing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : These little marks record a dance my feet might otherwise forget. | See #heelstamp# beside #toeline#?
b : Is that a heel there? | Is that one step or two?
a : Yes. The narrow end of the mark says which way the dancer had to turn. | One foot is resting and the other goes forward. Put two dark marks down and we'd stand still all night.

scene sheets
when topic=work self.job=scholar self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A leaf with a damp corner must lie flat until you can lift it cleanly. | I'd put a scrap under the corner of an old entry before turning it.
b : Won't it dry faster held up? | Does the scrap carry the weight?
a : It might tear faster too. I'd start by giving the ink a little air. | Just that of the corner. Then the whole leaf comes up on my palm.

scene price
when topic=prices self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I ask a price just once if I'm buying cider. | If looking into my purse alters the price I'll close the purse.
b : Even if it seems dear? | Mightn't the seller come down?
a : If it's dear I can leave the cup standing. No damage to the cider or my temper. | I might stay long enough to point out that I'd wanted the first price stated fairly.

scene mist
when topic=weather self.likes=misty_dawns
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In a misty morning an old street looks like a sentence rubbed half out. | I like seeing a roof emerge one clear line at a time.
b : Which bit comes back first? | Would you dance in that mist?
a : The bit one's nose is likeliest to strike. I save the poetry for after the walk. | If I could see the boards. The feet are entitled to an equally clear view.

scene cider
when topic=food self.likes=spiced_cider
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A strip of orange peel can hold a whole mouthful's worth of spice. | I drink the cider in small measures and leave the peel in plain sight.
b : Do you eat the peel? | Why see it?
a : The soft bit at the tip. That's the part that's been in the cup the longest. | To know whether it's still giving colour. It's a kind of warm, readable ink.

scene dryfoot
when topic=health self.dislikes=wet_floors
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep my foot flat and short on any floor that's been washed. | A wet heel makes a very complete signature on a dark board.
b : Isn't it slower? | Do you recognise the signature?
a : To the far wall, yes. To a warm bed instead of a broken leg, considerably faster. | Mine. The outside corner wears faster since I learnt a particular turning step.

scene market
when topic=pastimes self.likes=market_bustle
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd watch the feet of wolves at a busy market quite happily. | A line that moves around a puddle at market has a rhythm.
b : Not the goods? | Would you set it on paper?
a : On occasion. That crowded lane shows me turns nobody thought to put in a dance yet. | I have. The trick is to keep the hesitation when there's no actual puddle.

scene homewife
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a curve in one dancing figure I've saved to show #self.spouse#. | I'd lay a place for #self.spouse# at whichever end I've kept spotless.
b : Will it take two to make the figure? | What goes on the other side?
a : Two and room to turn. Drawing a solo figure makes those steps look rather lonesome. | Papers, cup marks, my little private litter. A shared meal deserves one clear start.

scene office
when topic=land self.quarter=office
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The Office looks quieter from outside than it sounds to a clerk. | There's music in doors opening up the Office corridor.
b : Is paper so loud? | Are the hinges singing?
a : It's the hush when three readers stop to find the same line. The paper makes a great rustle after that. | Mostly the footsteps on the way out. A matter settled makes a quick light tread.

scene unfiled
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't file a guess under another wolf's name. | A witness who only remembers an initial hasn't given me enough to go by.
b : Where would you file it then? | No helpful guess at all?
a : Among questions, until the answer can stand up in ink. | I could offer several. That's an excellent reason to offer none.

scene twolines
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Two wolves sitting quietly can give each other a great deal of room to think. | I sometimes repeat a prayer in the time of a walking song.
b : Is the quiet the important part? | Does the tune get in the way?
a : The company. Quiet without company has an entirely different weight. | Only if I let it hurry the words. I make the time fit what I mean to say.

scene freeberth
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A ship figures in my sleep, with one cabin perfectly free of damp. | I fancy hearing a sea song without the boards standing still under me.
b : Have you given yourself a grand cabin? | Would you be any use aboard?
a : Much too small for grandeur. Just space for dry paper and a narrow turn. | If somebody needs a steady record of just how much the deck is moving, certainly.

scene wineink
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't test the point of a new pen with my name. | There's a turning step at the top of each practice sheet.
b : What comes first? | Is it the same step?
a : An inked heel and two small strokes about it. If those are clean, the letters can have a turn. | It varies with the pen. A broad nib invites a step with rather more dignity.

scene friend
when topic=smalltalk self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd put #self.friend# near the front if there were a dance and I were handing out places. | I've a little square of clean margin for #self.friend# alone.
b : To lead the dancing? | What shall go in it?
a : To see clearly, if there's a wish to see. A front place offers a fine view. | Any tune that comes my way in good company. I needn't write the company down.

scene rich
when topic=prices self.wealth=rich
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can afford a whole sheet for a little thought. | A clerk with comfortable shoes has a choice in how far to walk with a caller.
b : Why use a scrap then? | Would you go beyond the office door?
a : Because sometimes I have only a scrap's worth to say. Wasting a page doesn't enlarge it. | If the proper office is hard to find, yes. No great hardship with sound soles and time.

scene borrowedwork
when topic=work self.job=scholar
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An erasure and a correction need different marks. | I leave the wrong turn showing when I correct a little map.
b : What should the reader see? | Why leave it visible?
a : That somebody has owned a mistake. Blotting it dark doesn't make the right answer clearer. | So the next reader can see exactly where a turn goes astray, and take the other.

scene fastbeat
when topic=pastimes self.likes=dancing
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A hurried tune tends to put the inkmarks close together. | I keep a blank strip down the side of every dance drawing.
b : Do the feet seem to crowd too? | What fills that strip?
a : So close they're likely to exchange complaints. I practise the turn slowly before taking the proper time. | My thumb. I can hold the sheet without covering the very step I wanted.

scene evenlamp
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A lamp brings a fine gold edge onto a damp line of ink. | Even after I've darkened the lamp I can still draw that dance perfectly well.
b : Is it ready to put away? | On paper you can't see?
a : Exactly the reverse. I leave it until the edge is dull. | On the floor, with my feet. They don't need a pen to remember their business.

story wrongmargin [topic=memories]
  : I once mistook my own note about a dance for a direction to the next shelf.
  : I went left twice, right once, made a very elegant turn and met precisely the shelf I'd started from.
  b : Did you find the paper you wanted?
  : Under my elbow. My feet had been the only things looking in the wrong place.

story ciderfoot [topic=food self.likes=spiced_cider]
  : I made a drawing with cider after my ink had dried in the well.
  : The pale picture vanished almost to nothing as I watched.
  b : Could you see it when the light changed?
  : Not well enough to dance it. The sheet smelt delightful, which I freely admit is unusual in a record.

story clearway [topic=travel]
  : On a particularly misty walk I reckoned the paces between each pair of familiar windows.
  : A loose stone made me take a much longer step, and the whole distance seemed to change.
  b : How did you set yourself straight?
  : Looked up. Somebody had left the last window open and the frame stood out plainly against the pale air.

rule @work
when concept=bark self.job=scholar self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep damp ink clear of the next leaf! | One blotting cloth for each fresh page.

rule @floor
when concept=bark self.dislikes=wet_floors
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Go flat-footed on the glossy board. | Leave a dry strip for the next caller.

rule @drink
when concept=bark self.likes=spiced_cider
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep the peel in for another breath. | No inkstand beside an open cup!

rule @lamps
when concept=bark here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Give the turning dancer an extra elbow. | Keep the lamp beyond the moving sleeve.

dlg @1 resident.hub : There's a moment between entries. What brings you?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : Welcome to the next line, #topic.player#.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I can hear a civil statement perfectly well from that distance.
dlg @4 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Draw closer to the legible side of the lamplight.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=scholar] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. I try to send a caller away with the right leaf, in readable condition.
dlg @2 resident.job : I sort what has been confused and mark the place where one may pick it up again.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : The account I've been given reads as follows. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : An easy turning step on your way.
graft @dance_margin resident.hub
choice May I try the steps in your margin? -> dance_margin
node dance_margin
say First put your heel on the fat mark. Turn your toes out and bring the other foot alongside. You've just covered the first line without moving much at all.
choice Where does the dancing begin? -> dance_margin_more
choice Rest the page beside the pen. -> hub
node dance_margin_more
say On the next beat. The first line persuades two wolves to face the same way. After that they can do something handsomer with the agreement.
choice Rest the page beside the pen. -> hub
choice Step back into the street. -> bye
